 "voice": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "t": 0.06666666666666667,
   "dur": 4.039,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "Which hand aged? Both belong to neighbours, under the same fierce sun."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 4.966666666666667,
   "dur": 11.811,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "In the early nineties, in a Queensland town called Nambour, chance decided who would wear sunscreen every morning. They put it on head, neck, arms and hands; neighbours used it as they pleased."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 18.033333333333335,
   "dur": 8.969,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "Then researchers read the fine lines in silicone casts of hands. After four and a half years, the daily group showed no detectable increase in ageing."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 28.3,
   "dur": 10.8,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "It's easy to think of sun damage as the burn you feel. But an ultraviolet camera picks up damage the naked eye misses, building long before anything shows on the surface."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 41.833333333333336,
   "dur": 9.168,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "Then the town was watched for ten more years. Squamous cell cancers had already come out lower, and melanoma came out at about half, in small numbers."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "t": 54.9,
   "dur": 5.52,
   "file": "vo/06.wav",
   "text": "At a lab's test dose, that morning layer is about a fifth of a paper's thickness."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "t": 61.43333333333333,
   "dur": 5.628,
   "file": "vo/07.wav",
   "text": "So, which hand aged? The eye can't say, but the skin was keeping its own record."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo08",
   "t": 67.96666666666667,
   "dur": 4.586,
   "file": "vo/08.wav",
   "text": "Next: tanning beds share a list with cigarettes. Same list, same risk?"
  }
 ]
